  "id": "COMPOUND:18027 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "Chloropeptin is implicated in the interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of molecular pathways. The evidence suggests that Chloropeptin acts as a target for ME-180, Sophoranochromene, and 2,2,2-Trideuterio-1-(2-hydroxy-4-methoxyphenyl)ethanone, all of which are known to target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This indicates that Chloropeptin may interact with the complex through a shared mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of these compounds. The presence of multiple pathways converging on the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex suggests a potential role for Chloropeptin in regulating gene expression via the polycomb group (PcG) pathway, which is involved in chromatin modification and gene silencing. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular interactions and underscores the importance of understanding how Chloropeptin might influence the function of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex in biological processes.",
